# tests/play.script - a game by keys (make test; tests/check.sh checks what it left).
# Time 0: the program started.
#  1. the title (any key), the main menu: PLAY NEW GAME (Enter)
6000 key space 100
11500 shot
12500 key enter 100
#  2. the map: the game saved (S, the first slot, the name HZTEST)
16000 key s 100
17000 shot
17500 key enter 100
18200 HZTEST\n
19500 shot
#  3. the map's paths (each move held until a wall stops it), past the journal (Enter
#     closes it), into level 1
20500 key down 1000
21600 key right 2600
24300 key up 600
25000 key right 1500
26500 shot
27500 key enter 100
28000 key right 1500
29600 key down 2500
32500 shot
#  4. level 1: right, a jump (Ctrl) across the water, a shot (Space), another jump, then
#     into the water: the hero dies and starts the level again
34000 key right 400
34500 down lctrl
34500 down right
35200 up lctrl
35600 up right
35700 shot
36000 key space 100
36300 shot
37000 key right 300
37500 down lctrl
37500 down right
38200 up lctrl
38600 up right
39000 shot
40000 key right 2000
42500 shot
45000 shot
#  5. Esc: the game's menu; Q: quit the game; the high scores (a key); the main menu
47000 key esc 100
48000 shot
48500 key q 100
50000 shot
51000 key space 100
#  6. LOAD GAME: the first slot (the map, where it was saved)
53000 key l 100
54000 shot
54500 key enter 100
60000 shot
